 least how many number of blocks are needed to partition a circular sequence into blocks whose sum is less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"K"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"By monotonicity, it is easy to get the length of maximal blocks which starts from 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Assume the block with minimal length is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and its length is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", it is obvious that whatever the blocks are, there must be a block that it starts in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". So, we can iterate over all the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", making it the start of a block, and calculate the number of blocks. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Notice that all the lengths of blocks is (non-strictly) greater than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", therefore the number of blocks we need is at most "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" / "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1. We need to iterate "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" times, but each time we can get the answer in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"chil