{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that when "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" varies, the valid range for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" also varies, but the range is monotone, so we can maintain how many times a number appears in linear time. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's easy to show that this algorithm runs for "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/b432c23d334e09047956d9416408ed84e7b9667078e9ccc415a7466093cfb2a5.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", by Master Theorem. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are some other people using segment trees. You can see a nice implement "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/526/submission/10584435"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"here"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":1},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/526/problem/G"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Spiders Evil Plan"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this task, we are given a tree and many queries. In each query, we are supposed to calculate the maximum total length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" paths with the constraint that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be covered. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the union of the paths (it contains nodes and edges)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), if  "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 1 , then there is always a method that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is connected."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":" ","src":"/editorial-assets/73a4b609b834b94cd2a04715d7c4c50e2e5f59463b313dde619d74975a2db6b7.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Further, we could get the following theorem:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For an unrooted tree, if it has 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" leaves, then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" paths can cover this tree completely."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"blockquote"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Proof for this theorem is that, if some edge "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not covered, we can interchange two paths, i.e. we change two paths "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the subtree of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the subtree of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":" ","src":"/editorial-assets/7d5c3ea1deded4e2df1c4b7aad49a430a9aa31054db53a048067dedb0a630327.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So a query ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") could be described as :"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" leaves in the tree, with node "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and maximize the total of weight of the edges in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a query ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), we can make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" the root. Then this task is how to choose the leaves. Note that we could select leaves one by one, every time we select the leaf which makes answer larger without selecting the others, as follow :"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":" ","src":"/editorial-assets/7ff42343ae8f578db2e1104cc78c2dba714c2b82946613ed2da52eeebae24d3c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"But if for every query we need to change the root, the time complexity cannot be accepted. Assuming the longest path in the tree is ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") , we could find that whatever the query is, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will contain either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" certainly."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":" ","src":"/editorial-assets/86b15662f462d707a158ff7d19e3360adeebcd3be272f39c10b80ac61ef6fc89.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, we just need to make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" the root in turn, and get the maximum answers. However, there is another problem : "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" may not be in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Like this :"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":" ","src":"/editorial-assets/887c4f8ecf5ade0fcaedfb93b24faa4c940fae9179594cbc489b7b0a66543ade.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"But it doesn't matter. We just need to link "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with the selected, and erase some leaf. Of course after erasing, the answer should be maximum. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":" ","src":"/editorial-assets/2f86c029b1cc25606e3d95325c7041e20ee316623164d1050c5a71da6fdcc42c.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thanks, for all of your excellent performance!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/17281"}